    "note": "candidate-004 — fixed the break you found (20 values + 15 labels + dark: garbled label boxes AND no animation). Root cause: with many points the x-axis labels packed CLOSER than their cell width, so the label rects OVERLAPPED. Overlapping rects corrupt placeRects' per-band cursor walk — that rendered the labels as tofu boxes AND broke the curtain layer (it stopped covering, so the chart showed fully from frame 0 = 'no animation'). Two fixes: (1) DECIMATE x-labels — show every k-th label, where k = ceil(widest-label-width / point-spacing), so kept labels never overlap (here: every 2nd → Jan·Mar·May·Jul·Smoke·sf·er·fg); (2) put labels in their OWN placeRects pack so a label collision can never corrupt the chart marks or the curtain again. Verified on YOUR exact input (dark, 20 vals, 15 labels): curtain covers at t=0, wipes cleanly, all 20 markers clean, decimated labels crisp. Re-checked 10 edge cases incl. 30 labels — all valid, overlay depth ≤12, and the 8-point default is unchanged (labels fit → all shown, no decimation). NOTE: your input had 20 values but only 15 labels — the last 5 points intentionally get no label (index-aligned).",
